MTM.htmlRoutes="<div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div><span>2L</span></div><div><div class=\"c\">Second Link (Tuas)</div><div class=\"c\">Malaysia-Singapore Second Link</div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><h4>Best For</h4><ul><li>Residents of western Johor (Iskandar Puteri, Gelang Patah)</li><li>Destinations in western Singapore (Jurong, Tuas)</li><li>Avoiding peak hour congestion at Causeway</li><li>Those who prefer shorter wait times</li></ul></div><div><h4>Key Details</h4><ul><li><span>Malaysian Toll (Car)</span><span>RM 9.70</span></li><li><span>Malaysian Toll (Motorbike)</span><span>RM 4.30</span></li><li><span>Operating Hours</span><span>24 hours</span></li><li><span>Bridge Length</span><span>1.9 km</span></li></ul></div><div><h4>Pros</h4><ul><li>Generally shorter immigration queues</li><li>Less congested during peak hours</li><li>Faster for western destinations</li></ul></div><div><h4>Cons</h4><ul><li>Higher toll cost than Causeway</li><li>Longer distance for central SG destinations</li><li>No public bus services available</li></ul></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div><span>WL</span></div><div><div class=\"c\">Woodlands Causeway</div><div class=\"c\">Johor-Singapore Causeway</div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><h4>Best For</h4><ul><li>Residents of central/eastern Johor (JB City, Taman Molek)</li><li>Destinations in central/north Singapore</li><li>Using public transport (buses, upcoming RTS)</li><li>Budget-conscious commuters (lower toll)</li></ul></div><div><h4>Key Details</h4><ul><li><span>Malaysian Toll (Car)</span><span>RM 2.90</span></li><li><span>Malaysian Toll (Motorbike)</span><span>RM 1.20</span></li><li><span>Operating Hours</span><span>24 hours</span></li><li><span>Causeway Length</span><span>1.1 km</span></li></ul></div><div><h4>Pros</h4><ul><li>Lower toll cost</li><li>Excellent public transport connections</li><li>RTS Link coming (Feb 2027)</li><li>Shorter for central Singapore</li></ul></div><div><h4>Cons</h4><ul><li>Very congested during peak hours</li><li>Longer wait times at immigration</li><li>Heavy traffic on Malaysian side</li></ul></div></div></div></div><div><h2>Cross-Border Bus Services</h2><div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div><div class=\"c\">Causeway Link</div><div class=\"c\">Malaysian operator</div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><h4>Popular Routes</h4><ul><li><div><span>CW1</span><p>JB Sentral ↔ Woodlands</p></div><div class=\"c\">RM 4.80</div></li><li><div><span>CW2</span><p>Larkin ↔ Kranji MRT</p></div><div class=\"c\">RM 4.80</div></li><li><div><span>CW3</span><p>Larkin ↔ Jurong East</p></div><div class=\"c\">RM 6.00</div></li><li><div><span>CW5</span><p>JB Sentral ↔ Jurong East</p></div><div class=\"c\">RM 6.00</div></li></ul></div><div><h4>Key Info</h4><ul><li>First bus: 5:30am / Last bus: ~11:30pm</li><li>Frequency: 10-20 mins (peak), 30 mins (off-peak)</li><li>Payment: Cash (RM/SGD) or EZ-Link/Touch n Go</li><li>Monthly pass available (~RM 180)</li></ul></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div><div class=\"c\">SBS Transit</div><div class=\"c\">Singapore public buses</div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><h4>Cross-Border Routes</h4><ul><li><div><span>Bus 170</span><p>Queen St ↔ Larkin</p></div><div class=\"c\">SGD 2.30</div></li><li><div><span>Bus 170X</span><p>Kranji ↔ Larkin (Express)</p></div><div class=\"c\">SGD 2.00</div></li></ul></div><div><h4>Key Info</h4><ul><li>Historic route since 1960s</li><li>First bus: 5:20am / Last bus: 11:20pm</li><li>Frequency: 8-15 mins (peak)</li><li>Payment: EZ-Link, NETS, Contactless</li><li>Connects to SG MRT network</li></ul></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div><div class=\"c\">Transtar Travel</div><div class=\"c\">Premium express service</div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><h4>Routes</h4><ul><li><div><span>TS1</span><p>JB Sentral ↔ Newton</p></div><div class=\"c\">SGD 6.00</div></li><li><div><span>TS3</span><p>JB Sentral ↔ Harbourfront</p></div><div class=\"c\">SGD 7.00</div></li><li><div><span>TS6</span><p>JB Sentral ↔ Changi Airport</p></div><div class=\"c\">SGD 10.00</div></li><li><div><span>TS8</span><p>JB Sentral ↔ Suntec City</p></div><div class=\"c\">SGD 6.00</div></li></ul></div><div><h4>Key Info</h4><ul><li>Premium express coach service</li><li>Fewer stops, faster journey</li><li>Online booking recommended</li><li>Monthly packages available</li></ul></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Bus Commuter Tips</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><h4>Immigration Process</h4><p>All passengers must alight at both Malaysia and Singapore checkpoints for immigration clearance, then re-board the same bus.</p></div><div><h4>Peak Hour Strategy</h4><p>Arrive 15-20 mins early during peak hours. Buses can fill up quickly, especially CW routes between 6:30-8:30am.</p></div><div><h4>Best Value</h4><p>SBS 170 offers the lowest fare but more stops. Causeway Link monthly passes offer best value for regular commuters.</p></div><div><h4>Luggage</h4><p>Most buses allow one piece of luggage. Large bags may incur extra charges. Transtar coaches have dedicated luggage storage.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Pro Tips for Daily Commuters</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><h4>Beat the Queue</h4><p>Leave before 6:30am or after 9:30am to avoid the worst morning traffic. Check live camera feeds before departing.</p></div><div><h4>Fuel Strategy</h4><p>Fill up in Malaysia where fuel is significantly cheaper. Singapore requires minimum 3/4 tank when leaving.</p></div><div><h4>Payment Setup</h4><p>Have both Touch n Go card and Singapore IU ready. Enable auto-reload to avoid balance issues at toll booths.</p></div><div><h4>Motorbike Option</h4><p>Motorbikes often have shorter queues and lower costs. VEP is only SGD 4 vs SGD 20-35 for cars. Many commuters use bikes specifically for border crossing.</p></div><div><h4>Flexible Working</h4><p>Negotiate flexible hours with your employer. Starting at 10am instead of 9am can save 30-45 minutes each way.</p></div><div><h4>Stay Updated</h4><p>Follow One Motoring and JPJ social media for real-time updates on traffic and any checkpoint issues.</p></div></div></div></div>";
MTM.htmlQR="<div><div><h2>QR Code Immigration &amp; MACS</h2><p>Speed up your border crossing with digital immigration clearance. Here's everything you need to know about MyNIISe, myICA, and MACS.</p></div><div><div><p>Always carry your passport</p><p>Even with digital QR codes and apps, you <span>must</span> carry your physical passport at all times when crossing the border. Immigration officers may request it for verification, and it remains a legal requirement for international travel.</p></div></div><div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">MyNIISe (New Immigration Integrated System Environment)</div><div class=\"c\">Malaysia's QR code immigration app by Jabatan Imigresen Malaysia</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><h4> What is MyNIISe?</h4><p>MyNIISe is the Malaysian Immigration Department's (Jabatan Imigresen Malaysia) official mobile app for digital immigration services. It enables QR code-based clearance at Malaysian checkpoints, allowing faster and contactless processing on the Malaysia side.</p></div><div><h4>Key Features</h4><ul><li><span>QR Code Clearance:</span> Generate a QR code for immigration scanning, so no physical passport stamp is needed</li><li><span>Digital Travel Record:</span> Your entry/exit records are stored digitally in the system</li><li><span>Passport Registration:</span> Register your passport within the app for quick retrieval</li><li><span>Multi-user Support:</span> Register family members' passports under one account</li></ul></div><div><h4>How to Set Up</h4><ol><li>Download the MyNIISe app from the App Store or Google Play</li><li>Create an account and verify your identity</li><li>Register your passport within the app</li><li>Generate a QR code before approaching immigration</li><li>Scan the QR code at designated MyNIISe lanes at the checkpoint</li></ol></div><div><h4>Who Can Use It?</h4><ul><li>Malaysian citizens</li><li>Singapore citizens crossing at Johor checkpoints</li><li>Other eligible foreign nationals</li></ul></div><div><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/sg/app/myniise/id6744350770\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">📱 App Store</a><a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=my.gov.onegovappstore.niise\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">📱 Google Play</a></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">myICA Mobile App</div><div class=\"c\">Singapore's official immigration app by the Immigration &amp; Checkpoints Authority</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><h4> What is myICA?</h4><p>myICA is Singapore's Immigration &amp; Checkpoints Authority (ICA) official mobile app. It serves as your digital companion for all Singapore immigration matters, including submitting arrival cards and storing electronic visit passes.</p></div><div><h4>Key Features</h4><ul><li><span>SG Arrival Card (SGAC):</span> Submit your arrival declaration digitally up to 3 days before travel</li><li><span>QR Code Storage:</span> View and store your immigration QR codes for easy scanning</li><li><span>Travel History:</span> Access your entry/exit records digitally</li><li><span>e-Pass:</span> Receive electronic visit passes instead of physical stamps</li></ul></div><div><h4>How to Set Up</h4><ol><li>Download the myICA app from the App Store or Google Play</li><li>Create an account using your passport details</li><li>Complete the SG Arrival Card (SGAC) before your trip</li><li>Save your QR code for quick access at immigration</li><li>Use the QR code at automated immigration lanes in Singapore</li></ol></div><div><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/myica-mobile/id1584952674\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">📱 App Store</a><a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=sg.gov.ica.mobile.app\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">📱 Google Play</a></div><div><p>Pro Tip for Daily Commuters</p><p>The SGAC is valid for 3 days. Regular commuters should save their QR code for quick access and update their SGAC every 3 days.</p></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">MACS (Malaysia Automated Clearance System)</div><div class=\"c\">Malaysia's autogate system for non-Malaysian frequent travellers at Johor land checkpoints</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><h4>What is MACS?</h4><p>MACS is Malaysia's automated border clearance system designed specifically for <span>non-Malaysian</span> frequent travellers. Upon registration, a MACS sticker (or stamp) is affixed to your passport, enabling you to use autogate lanes at both the Causeway (BSI) and Second Link (KSAB) checkpoints.</p></div><div><h4>Eligibility</h4><ul><li>Singapore citizens</li><li>Singapore Permanent Residents</li><li>Long-term pass holders commuting through Johor land checkpoints</li></ul></div></div><div><h4>Fee &amp; Validity</h4><p><span>RM30</span> for one-year validity. The MACS sticker or stamp is affixed to your passport upon registration at the immigration office.</p></div><div><h4>How to Use MACS</h4><ol><li>Register and obtain a MACS sticker on your passport at the immigration office</li><li>Look for the designated autogate lanes at Malaysian immigration</li><li>Scan the data page of your passport on the reader</li><li>Place your finger on the biometric scanner for verification</li><li>Look at the camera for facial recognition</li><li>The gate opens automatically once verification is complete</li></ol></div><div><h4>💡 What About Malaysian Citizens?</h4><p>Malaysians do <span>not</span> use MACS. Instead, Malaysian citizens use <span>automated e-gates</span> (autogates) for entry and exit at Malaysian checkpoints using their biometric passport or MyKad.</p></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Quick Comparison</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>MyNIISe (MY)</th><th>myICA App</th><th>MACS (MY)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Country</td><td>Malaysia</td><td>Singapore</td><td>Malaysia</td></tr><tr><td>Method</td><td>Mobile app QR code</td><td>Mobile app QR</td><td>Passport + biometrics</td></tr><tr><td>Pre-registration</td><td>App download required</td><td>App download required</td><td>MACS sticker/stamp (RM30/year)</td></tr><tr><td>Passport Stamp</td><td>No (digital record)</td><td>No (e-Pass)</td><td>No (digital record)</td></tr><tr><td>Best For</td><td>QR clearance at MY checkpoints</td><td>Pre-arrival declaration &amp; record keeping</td><td>Non-Malaysian frequent travellers (SG citizens, PRs, long-term pass holders)</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div>";
MTM.htmlPropInfo="<div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Renting in Johor Bahru</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><h3>Typical Rental Process</h3><ol><li><span>1</span><span>Search for properties on PropertyGuru, iProperty, or through agents</span></li><li><span>2</span><span>Schedule viewings and inspect the property thoroughly</span></li><li><span>3</span><span>Negotiate rental terms and monthly rate</span></li><li><span>4</span><span>Sign the Letter of Intent (LOI) with 1 month's deposit</span></li><li><span>5</span><span>Sign the Tenancy Agreement (typically 1-2 year terms)</span></li><li><span>6</span><span>Pay security deposit (2 months) + utility deposit (0.5 months)</span></li><li><span>7</span><span>Collect keys and complete inventory checklist</span></li></ol></div><div><div><h4>What's Usually Included</h4><ul><li>Air-conditioning units</li><li>Basic kitchen appliances</li><li>Water heater</li><li>Built-in wardrobes</li><li>Maintenance of common areas</li></ul></div><div><h4>Watch Out For</h4><ul><li>Unclear utility bill arrangements</li><li>Missing inventory documentation</li><li>Maintenance responsibility disputes</li><li>Early termination penalties</li><li>Unclear parking arrangements</li></ul></div></div><div><h3>Typical Monthly Rentals (2024)</h3><div><div><p>Studio/1BR Condo</p><p>RM 1,000 - 1,800</p></div><div><p>2BR Condo</p><p>RM 1,500 - 2,500</p></div><div><p>3BR Condo</p><p>RM 2,000 - 3,500</p></div><div><p>Terrace House</p><p>RM 1,200 - 2,500</p></div><div><p>Semi-D</p><p>RM 2,500 - 5,000</p></div><div><p>Bungalow</p><p>RM 4,000 - 10,000+</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Buying Property in Malaysia</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><h4>Foreigners Can Buy Property</h4><p>Malaysia allows foreigners to purchase property, subject to minimum price thresholds that vary by state. In Johor, the minimum is typically RM 1 million for landed property and RM 500,000 for condominiums in certain areas.</p></div><div><h3>Property Types</h3><div><div><div><p>Condominium</p><div class=\"c\">RM 300K - 1.5M</div></div><p>High-rise with facilities, lower maintenance</p></div><div><div><p>Apartment</p><div class=\"c\">RM 150K - 500K</div></div><p>Mid-rise, more affordable, basic facilities</p></div><div><div><p>Terrace House</p><div class=\"c\">RM 400K - 1M</div></div><p>Landed, 2-3 storeys, row housing</p></div><div><div><p>Semi-Detached</p><div class=\"c\">RM 700K - 2M</div></div><p>Landed, shares one wall with neighbour</p></div><div><div><p>Bungalow</p><div class=\"c\">RM 1.5M - 5M+</div></div><p>Standalone landed, premium pricing</p></div><div><div><p>Cluster Home</p><div class=\"c\">RM 600K - 1.5M</div></div><p>Landed within gated strata development</p></div></div></div><div><h3>Buying Costs to Budget For</h3><div><div><div><span>Down Payment</span></div><span>10-20% of purchase price</span></div><div><div><span>Stamp Duty</span></div><span>1-4% depending on property value</span></div><div><div><span>Legal Fees</span></div><span>0.4-1% of purchase price</span></div><div><div><span>Valuation Fee</span></div><span>RM 500 - 2,000</span></div><div><div><span>Loan Processing</span></div><span>Varies by bank</span></div></div></div><div><h3>Buying Process Timeline</h3><ol><li><span>1</span><div><span>Property Search &amp; Viewing</span><div class=\"c\">2-8 weeks</div></div></li><li><span>2</span><div><span>Letter of Offer &amp; Booking Fee</span><div class=\"c\">1-2 days</div></div></li><li><span>3</span><div><span>Loan Application &amp; Approval</span><div class=\"c\">2-4 weeks</div></div></li><li><span>4</span><div><span>Sign Sale &amp; Purchase Agreement (SPA)</span><div class=\"c\">14 days after booking</div></div></li><li><span>5</span><div><span>Pay Balance (minus loan amount)</span><div class=\"c\">3 months from SPA</div></div></li><li><span>6</span><div><span>Title Transfer &amp; Key Collection</span><div class=\"c\">1-3 months</div></div></li></ol></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div class=\"c\">Legal Considerations</div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><h3>Key Documents</h3><div><div><p>Sale and Purchase Agreement (SPA)</p><p>Main contract for property purchase, typically 3+1 format</p></div><div><p>Tenancy Agreement</p><p>Rental contract, usually stamped at LHDN for legal validity</p></div><div><p>Letter of Intent / Offer</p><p>Initial booking document before formal agreement</p></div><div><p>Title Deed / Strata Title</p><p>Proof of property ownership</p></div><div><p>Developer's License</p><p>For new developments, verify with KPKT</p></div></div></div><div><h4>Important for Foreigners</h4><ul><li>State consent may be required for certain property purchases</li><li>MM2H visa holders have different thresholds</li><li>Malay Reserved Land cannot be purchased by non-Malays</li><li>Agricultural land has restrictions for foreign buyers</li><li>Always engage a licensed property lawyer</li></ul></div><div><h3>Minimum Price for Foreigners in Johor</h3><div><div><p>Landed Property</p><p>RM 1,000,000</p><p>Terrace, Semi-D, Bungalow</p></div><div><p>High-Rise / Condo</p><p>RM 500,000</p><p>In designated zones</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>";
MTM.htmlSez={"overview": "<div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">What is the JS-SEZ?</div></div><div class=\"c\"><p>The <span>Johor-Singapore Special Economic Zone (JS-SEZ)</span> is a landmark bilateral initiative between Malaysia and Singapore, designed to create an integrated cross-border economic region. It builds upon the existing Iskandar Malaysia economic corridor, adding a new layer of bilateral cooperation covering tax incentives, customs facilitation, talent mobility, and coordinated industrial policy.</p><p>The vision: combine Johor's abundant land, competitive labour costs, and strategic location with Singapore's world-class financial infrastructure, deep capital markets, and global connectivity, creating a combined economic region greater than the sum of its parts.</p><div><div><div>~2,217 km²</div><p>Iskandar Malaysia region covered by JS-SEZ framework</p></div><div><div>RM 400B+</div><p>Cumulative committed investment in Iskandar Malaysia (2006–2024)</p></div><div><div>5 mins</div><p>JB to Singapore via RTS Link (February 2027)</p></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Key Milestones &amp; Timeline</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><div><div></div><div><span>2006</span><p>Iskandar Malaysia (formerly IDR) established as Malaysia's first economic corridor</p></div></div><div><div></div><div><span>2012</span><p>Medini Iskandar designated as an international financial and business district</p></div></div><div><div></div><div><span>2018</span><p>Forest City declared a duty-free island and financial hub</p></div></div><div><div></div><div><span>2023</span><p>JS-SEZ concept formalised in Joint Leaders' Statement between Malaysia &amp; Singapore</p></div></div><div><div></div><div><span>2024</span><p>JS-SEZ Agreement signed; framework for cross-border economic cooperation takes shape</p></div></div><div><div></div><div><span>2025</span><p>Implementation details being finalised: tax incentives, customs facilitation, governance structure</p></div></div><div><div></div><div><span>2027</span><p>RTS Link opens in February, physically connecting Johor Bahru to Singapore's MRT network</p></div></div><div><div></div><div><span>2030+</span><p>Full maturation of JS-SEZ ecosystem, the target for major multinational presence and cross-border workforce</p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Target Sectors</div><div class=\"c\">Priority industries being developed within the JS-SEZ framework</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><h4>Financial Services &amp; Fintech</h4><p>Banking, insurance, digital payments, and family offices leveraging proximity to Singapore</p></div><div><h4>Technology &amp; Digital Economy</h4><p>Data centres, AI/ML, cybersecurity, and SaaS companies seeking cost-effective ASEAN bases</p></div><div><h4>Advanced Manufacturing</h4><p>Semiconductors, aerospace components, precision engineering, and EV supply chains</p></div><div><h4>Logistics &amp; Supply Chain</h4><p>Leveraging PTP, Senai Airport, and cross-border facilitation for regional distribution</p></div><div><h4>Professional Services</h4><p>Legal, accounting, consulting, and HR firms serving cross-border businesses</p></div><div><h4>Healthcare &amp; Biotech</h4><p>Medical tourism, pharmaceutical manufacturing, and health-tech innovation</p></div></div></div></div></div>", "zones": "<div><p>The JS-SEZ encompasses <span>nine flagship zones</span> across southern Johor. Each zone has distinct economic specialisations and advantages.</p><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><span>A</span>Johor Baru City Centre</div><div class=\"c\">The urban core and traditional commercial hub. RTS Link terminus connecting directly to Singapore's Woodlands North MRT station.</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><h4>Key Highlights</h4><ul><li>RTS Link terminal (Feb 2027)</li><li>CIQ complexes</li><li>Heritage &amp; culture district</li></ul></div><div><h4>Focus Sectors</h4><div><div class=\"c\">Business services</div><div class=\"c\">Digital economy</div><div class=\"c\">Health</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><span>B</span>Iskandar Puteri</div><div class=\"c\">Administrative capital of Iskandar Malaysia, home to Medini, the designated financial and business district with special tax incentives.</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><h4>Key Highlights</h4><ul><li>Medini duty-free zone</li><li>LEGOLAND &amp; EduCity</li><li>Puteri Harbour waterfront</li></ul></div><div><h4>Focus Sectors</h4><div><div class=\"c\">Manufacturing</div><div class=\"c\">Business services</div><div class=\"c\">Digital economy</div><div class=\"c\">Education</div><div class=\"c\">Health</div><div class=\"c\">Tourism</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><span>C</span>Tanjung Pelepas – Tanjung Bin</div><div class=\"c\">Major port and industrial corridor. Port of Tanjung Pelepas (PTP) is among the world's top transhipment hubs.</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><h4>Key Highlights</h4><ul><li>PTP, a top 20 global port</li><li>Southern Industrial &amp; Logistics Clusters (SILC)</li><li>Free Trade Zone</li></ul></div><div><h4>Focus Sectors</h4><div><div class=\"c\">Manufacturing</div><div class=\"c\">Energy</div><div class=\"c\">Logistics</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><span>D</span>Pasir Gudang</div><div class=\"c\">Heavy industry and petrochemical zone with deep-water port access and established industrial estates.</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><h4>Key Highlights</h4><ul><li>Pasir Gudang Port</li><li>Tanjung Langsat Industrial Complex</li><li>Oil &amp; gas facilities</li></ul></div><div><h4>Focus Sectors</h4><div><div class=\"c\">Manufacturing</div><div class=\"c\">Energy</div><div class=\"c\">Logistics</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><span>E</span>Senai-Skudai</div><div class=\"c\">Aerospace and high-tech manufacturing hub anchored by Senai International Airport and the Senai Hi-Tech Park.</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><h4>Key Highlights</h4><ul><li>Senai Airport city</li><li>Senai Hi-Tech Park</li><li>i-Park (industrial park)</li></ul></div><div><h4>Focus Sectors</h4><div><div class=\"c\">Manufacturing</div><div class=\"c\">Digital economy</div><div class=\"c\">Education</div><div class=\"c\">Logistics</div><div class=\"c\">Tourism</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><span>F</span>Sedenak</div><div class=\"c\">Emerging tech and industrial hub positioned as a future growth node for manufacturing, digital economy, and energy sectors.</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><h4>Key Highlights</h4><ul><li>Sedenak Tech Valley</li><li>Data centre corridor</li><li>Green energy initiatives</li></ul></div><div><h4>Focus Sectors</h4><div><div class=\"c\">Manufacturing</div><div class=\"c\">Business services</div><div class=\"c\">Digital economy</div><div class=\"c\">Education</div><div class=\"c\">Energy</div><div class=\"c\">Food security</div><div class=\"c\">Health</div><div class=\"c\">Logistics</div><div class=\"c\">Tourism</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><span>G</span>Forest City</div><div class=\"c\">Purpose-built smart city and designated Special Financial Zone (SFZ) with duty-free status, attracting global financial services and family offices.</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><h4>Key Highlights</h4><ul><li>Special Financial Zone status</li><li>Duty-free island</li><li>Integrated smart city</li></ul></div><div><h4>Focus Sectors</h4><div><div class=\"c\">Financial services</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><span>H</span>Pengerang Integrated Petroleum Complex (PIPC)</div><div class=\"c\">Southeast Asia's largest integrated oil and gas complex, anchored by PETRONAS' RAPID refinery and petrochemical facilities.</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><h4>Key Highlights</h4><ul><li>PETRONAS RAPID complex</li><li>Deep-water terminal</li><li>Petrochemical integration</li></ul></div><div><h4>Focus Sectors</h4><div><div class=\"c\">Manufacturing</div><div class=\"c\">Energy</div><div class=\"c\">Logistics</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><span>I</span>Desaru</div><div class=\"c\">Coastal tourism and wellness destination on Johor's southeastern tip, with a growing focus on education, food security, and healthcare.</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><h4>Key Highlights</h4><ul><li>Desaru Coast resort hub</li><li>Eco-tourism corridor</li><li>Agricultural zone</li></ul></div><div><h4>Focus Sectors</h4><div><div class=\"c\">Education</div><div class=\"c\">Food security</div><div class=\"c\">Health</div><div class=\"c\">Tourism</div></div></div></div></div></div></div>", "incentives": "<div><div><p>JS-SEZ-specific incentive details are still being finalised. The incentives below reflect existing Iskandar Malaysia / Medini frameworks and expected JS-SEZ enhancements based on official announcements.</p></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Tax Incentives</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><p>Corporate tax rate as low as 0–5% for qualifying activities in designated zones</p></div><div><p>Income tax exemptions or reductions for knowledge workers and C-suite talent</p></div><div><p>Stamp duty exemptions on property transfers within JS-SEZ zones</p></div><div><p>Import duty &amp; sales tax exemptions for raw materials and machinery</p></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Business Facilitation</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div><p>Streamlined business registration and licensing via one-stop centre (OSC)</p></div><div><p>Relaxed foreign ownership rules, with up to 100% foreign equity in many sectors</p></div><div><p>Fast-track work permits and employment passes for skilled professionals</p></div><div><p>Dedicated customs facilitation for cross-border trade with Singapore</p></div></div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Johor vs Singapore: Cost Comparison</div><div class=\"c\">Indicative comparison for businesses considering Johor as an alternative or complement to Singapore operations</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Factor</div><div class=\"c\">Johor (JS-SEZ)</div><div class=\"c\">Singapore</div></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Grade A office rent (per sq ft/month)</div><div class=\"c\">RM 3–6 (~SGD 1–1.50)</div><div class=\"c\">SGD 8–15</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Corporate tax rate</div><div class=\"c\">0–5% (qualifying) / 24% (standard)</div><div class=\"c\">17%</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Average graduate salary (monthly)</div><div class=\"c\">RM 3,000–5,000</div><div class=\"c\">SGD 4,000–6,000</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Industrial land (per sq ft)</div><div class=\"c\">RM 15–40</div><div class=\"c\">SGD 200–600 (lease)</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Foreign ownership</div><div class=\"c\">Up to 100% in most sectors</div><div class=\"c\">100%</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>", "family-offices": "<div><p>Malaysia, and Johor in particular, is emerging as a destination for family offices looking for cost-efficient, strategically located bases near Singapore's financial ecosystem.</p><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Why Johor for Family Offices?</div></div><div class=\"c\"><ul><li><span>Proximity to Singapore's financial ecosystem without Singapore's cost base</span></li><li><span>Malaysia's Labuan IBFC offers tax-efficient structures (3% effective tax rate on trading income)</span></li><li><span>Forest City and Medini provide purpose-built financial districts</span></li><li><span>Lower operational costs, with office space at 30–50% of Singapore's rates</span></li><li><span>Access to ASEAN markets with Malaysia's bilateral tax treaties (70+ countries)</span></li></ul></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Emerging Structures</div></div><div class=\"c\"><ul><li><span>Single Family Offices (SFOs), managing wealth for one ultra-high-net-worth family</span></li><li><span>Multi-Family Offices (MFOs), sharing infrastructure serving multiple families</span></li><li><span>Labuan entities, popular for holding companies, IP management, and fund structures</span></li><li><span>Malaysia's Securities Commission (SC) is developing a dedicated family office framework</span></li><li><span>Potential tie-ups between Malaysian and Singapore-based family offices for cross-border strategies</span></li></ul></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Key Considerations</div></div><div class=\"c\"><ul><li><span>Regulatory clarity still evolving, so work with licensed advisors familiar with both Malaysian and Singapore regulations</span></li><li><span>Talent pipeline: access to bilingual professionals (English, Mandarin, Malay) for regional operations</span></li><li><span>Lifestyle appeal: international schools, healthcare, and low cost of living attract principals and staff</span></li><li><span>MM2H or PVIP visas can complement family office residency needs</span></li><li><span>Forest City's special financial zone status may unlock additional incentives for qualifying family offices</span></li></ul></div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Forest City Special Financial Zone</div></div><div class=\"c\"><p>Forest City has been designated as a special financial zone with duty-free status, positioning it as a potential hub for family offices and financial services within the JS-SEZ framework.</p><ul><li>Duty-free status on selected goods</li><li>Proposed incentives for financial services firms and family offices</li><li>Purpose-built Grade A office space at competitive rates</li><li>Integrated living: residential, commercial, and leisure in one development</li><li>Direct connectivity to Singapore via Second Link expressway</li></ul></div></div></div>", "news": "<div><p>Curated articles and reports covering the latest JS-SEZ developments, from policy announcements to industry analysis.</p><div><a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-01-06/singapore-malaysia-to-finalize-deal-creating-vast-economic-zone\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div class=\"c\">Policy</div><span>Jan 2025</span></div><div class=\"c\">Singapore, Malaysia Ink Deal Creating New Vast Economic Zone</div><p>Bloomberg</p></div><div class=\"c\"><p>Both nations aim to promote 100 projects in the first ten years, with tax breaks as the main draw for the new economic zone.</p></div></div></a><a href=\"https://asia.nikkei.com/economy/malaysia-seeks-to-revive-forest-city-ghost-town-as-financial-hub\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div class=\"c\">Finance</div><span>Nov 2024</span></div><div class=\"c\">Malaysia Seeks to Revive Forest City as Financial Hub</div><p>Nikkei Asia</p></div><div class=\"c\"><p>How Forest City's Special Financial Zone designation aims to woo family offices with tax perks and revive the stalled mega-project near the JS-SEZ.</p></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.straitstimes.com/business/economy/win-win-for-spore-and-malaysia-hope-and-caution-in-johor-as-rts-link-takes-shape\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div class=\"c\">Infrastructure</div><span>2025</span></div><div class=\"c\">RTS Link Set to Open by End of 2026: Win-Win for Singapore and Malaysia?</div><p>The Straits Times</p></div><div class=\"c\"><p>Hope and caution in Johor as the cross-border rapid transit system takes shape, promising to transform commuting and business connectivity.</p></div></div></a><a href=\"https://asia.nikkei.com/spotlight/asean-money/johor-singapore-special-economic-zone-gathers-investor-momentum\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div class=\"c\">Industry</div><span>2025</span></div><div class=\"c\">JS-SEZ Gathers Investor Momentum</div><p>Nikkei Asia</p></div><div class=\"c\"><p>Overview of growing investor interest and infrastructure progress in the Johor-Singapore Special Economic Zone.</p></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.pwc.com/my/en/services/tax/johor-singapore-special-economic-zone.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div class=\"c\">Tax &amp; Legal</div><span>2025</span></div><div class=\"c\">JS-SEZ: Tax Incentives &amp; Business Growth Opportunities</div><p>PwC Malaysia</p></div><div class=\"c\"><p>Detailed overview of tax holidays, investment tax allowances, and customs exemptions available under the JS-SEZ framework.</p></div></div></a><a href=\"https://scmp.com/week-asia/opinion/article/3304356/data-centres-are-booming-malaysias-johor-now-comes-hard-part-job-creation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div class=\"c\">Technology</div><span>Mar 2025</span></div><div class=\"c\">Data Centres Are Booming in Johor, and Now Comes the Hard Part</div><p>South China Morning Post</p></div><div class=\"c\"><p>How hyperscalers are transforming Johor's Sedenak corridor into Southeast Asia's largest data centre cluster, and the challenges of job creation.</p></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.businesstimes.com.sg/international/asean/singapore-based-firms-commit-over-s5-5-billion-investments-johor-after-js-sez-deal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div class=\"c\">Business</div><span>Jan 2025</span></div><div class=\"c\">Singapore-Based Firms Commit Over S$5.5 Billion in Johor After JS-SEZ Deal</div><p>Business Times</p></div><div class=\"c\"><p>Growing trend of Singapore SMEs and MNCs setting up operations in Johor to leverage lower costs while maintaining Singapore HQ functions.</p></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.channelnewsasia.com/today/big-read/johor-singapore-special-economic-zone-promise-challenges-5158506\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div class=\"c\">Analysis</div><span>2025</span></div><div class=\"c\">How the JS-SEZ Is Shaping Up to Be Different from Past Collaborations</div><p>Channel News Asia</p></div><div class=\"c\"><p>In-depth analysis of how the JS-SEZ framework addresses earlier shortcomings with stronger bilateral cooperation and early gains for businesses.</p></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.thestar.com.my/business/business-news/2025/02/13/js-sez-expected-to-spur-growth-in-eight-sectors\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div class=\"c\">Industry</div><span>Feb 2025</span></div><div class=\"c\">JS-SEZ Expected to Spur Growth in Eight Sectors</div><p>The Star</p></div><div class=\"c\"><p>Breakdown of the eight key sectors expected to benefit most from the JS-SEZ, including manufacturing, logistics, and financial services.</p></div></div></a><a href=\"https://www.channelnewsasia.com/asia/johor-singapore-sez-special-passes-industry-captains-could-ease-manpower-and-congestion-concerns-suggests-johor-chief-minister-4548381\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div><div class=\"c\">Policy</div><span>2025</span></div><div class=\"c\">JS-SEZ: Special Passes for 'Industry Captains' Could Ease Manpower Concerns</div><p>Channel News Asia</p></div><div class=\"c\"><p>Proposed changes to work permit frameworks that could allow seamless cross-border employment between Johor and Singapore within the SEZ.</p></div></div></a></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><p>Articles are curated for relevance. For the latest official updates, visit <a href=\"https://www.irda.com.my\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRDA</a>, <a href=\"https://www.mida.gov.my\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MIDA</a>, or <a href=\"https://www.mof.gov.my\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MOF Malaysia</a>.</p></div></div></div>", "faq": "<div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\">Frequently Asked Questions</div></div><div class=\"c\"><div class=\"c\"><details class=\"acc\"><summary>What exactly is the JS-SEZ?</summary><div class=\"acc-b\">The Johor-Singapore Special Economic Zone is a bilateral economic initiative between Malaysia and Singapore to create a seamless cross-border economic zone. It aims to combine Johor's land, labour, and cost advantages with Singapore's capital, technology, and global connectivity.</div></details><details class=\"acc\"><summary>How is the JS-SEZ different from Iskandar Malaysia?</summary><div class=\"acc-b\">Iskandar Malaysia is a Malaysian-only economic corridor established in 2006. The JS-SEZ builds on Iskandar's infrastructure but adds a bilateral dimension with Singapore, including coordinated tax incentives, customs facilitation, and cross-border workforce arrangements.</div></details><details class=\"acc\"><summary>Can I set up a company in the JS-SEZ as a foreigner?</summary><div class=\"acc-b\">Yes. Many sectors allow 100% foreign equity. The JS-SEZ is specifically designed to attract foreign investment with streamlined registration, tax incentives, and fast-track work permits. Certain sectors may have additional licensing requirements.</div></details><details class=\"acc\"><summary>What visa do I need to work in the JS-SEZ?</summary><div class=\"acc-b\">Employees typically need an Employment Pass (EP) sponsored by their employer. Business owners may apply for an EP or use an MM2H/PVIP visa if they meet the criteria. The JS-SEZ may introduce special visa categories as implementation progresses.</div></details><details class=\"acc\"><summary>When will the JS-SEZ be fully operational?</summary><div class=\"acc-b\">The framework was signed in 2024, with implementation details being finalised throughout 2025. Many incentives in Iskandar Malaysia already apply. Full JS-SEZ-specific incentives and governance are expected to roll out progressively from 2025–2027.</div></details><details class=\"acc\"><summary>Is Forest City part of the JS-SEZ?</summary><div class=\"acc-b\">Forest City sits within the Iskandar Malaysia region and has been designated as a special financial zone with duty-free status. It is expected to play a significant role in the JS-SEZ, particularly for financial services and family offices.</div></details><details class=\"acc\"><summary>How will the RTS Link affect the JS-SEZ?</summary><div class=\"acc-b\">The Rapid Transit System (RTS) Link, opening in February 2027, will connect JB Sentral to Singapore's Woodlands North MRT station in about 5 minutes. This dramatically reduces cross-border commute friction and is a key enabler for the JS-SEZ workforce model.</div></details></div></div></div></div>"};
